# List03 单词


## episode
- **音标**: /ˈepɪsoʊd/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 一段经历；插曲；一集
- **例句**: This episode changed his life forever.
- **近义词**: event, incident
- **派生词**: episodic (adj.)

## equal
- **音标**: /ˈiːkwəl/
- **词性**: adj. v. n.
- **释义**: 相等的；平等的；等于
- **例句**: All citizens are equal before the law.
- **近义词**: identical, equivalent
- **派生词**: equality (n.)

## equip
- **音标**: /ɪˈkwɪp/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 装备；配备
- **例句**: The lab is equipped with modern instruments.
- **近义词**: furnish, supply
- **派生词**: equipment (n.)

## equivalent
- **音标**: /ɪˈkwɪvələnt/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 等价的；相当的；等价物
- **例句**: One mile is equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.
- **近义词**: equal, comparable
- **派生词**: equivalence (n.)

## era
- **音标**: /ˈɪrə/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 时代；纪元
- **例句**: We are living in the digital era.
- **近义词**: age, period
- **派生词**: —

## error
- **音标**: /ˈerər/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 错误；过失
- **例句**: There was an error in the calculation.
- **近义词**: mistake, fault
- **派生词**: erroneous (adj.)

## escape
- **音标**: /ɪˈskeɪp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 逃跑；逃避
- **例句**: The prisoners escaped from the jail.
- **近义词**: flee, avoid
- **派生词**: —

## essential
- **音标**: /ɪˈsenʃl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 必要的；本质的；要素
- **例句**: Water is essential for life.
- **近义词**: vital, crucial
- **派生词**: essentially (adv.)

## establish
- **音标**: /ɪˈstæblɪʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 建立；确立
- **例句**: The university was established in 1900.
- **近义词**: found, create
- **派生词**: establishment (n.)

## estimate
- **音标**: /ˈestɪmeɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 估计；估算
- **例句**: The cost is estimated at $5000.
- **近义词**: assess, approximate
- **派生词**: estimation (n.)

## evaluate
- **音标**: /ɪˈvæljueɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 评估；评价
- **例句**: We need to evaluate the results carefully.
- **近义词**: assess, appraise
- **派生词**: evaluation (n.)

## evidence
- **音标**: /ˈevɪdəns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 证据；证明
- **例句**: There is no evidence to support this claim.
- **近义词**: proof, testimony
- **派生词**: evident (adj.)

## evolve
- **音标**: /ɪˈvɒlv/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 进化；发展
- **例句**: Technology has evolved rapidly in recent years.
- **近义词**: develop, progress
- **派生词**: evolution (n.)

## exceed
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsiːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 超过；超越
- **例句**: The results exceeded our expectations.
- **近义词**: surpass, outdo
- **派生词**: excessive (adj.)

## exception
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsepʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 例外
- **例句**: Everyone must follow the rules without exception.
- **近义词**: exclusion, anomaly
- **派生词**: exceptional (adj.)

## excess
- **音标**: /ɪkˈses/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 过量；过度的
- **例句**: An excess of sugar is bad for health.
- **近义词**: surplus, extra
- **派生词**: excessive (adj.)

## exclude
- **音标**: /ɪkˈskluːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 排除；排斥
- **例句**: The price excludes tax and delivery charges.
- **近义词**: omit, bar
- **派生词**: exclusion (n.)

## execute
- **音标**: /ˈeksɪkjuːt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 执行；处决
- **例句**: The plan was executed perfectly.
- **近义词**: perform, carry out
- **派生词**: execution (n.)

## exhibit
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 展示；展览
- **例句**: The museum exhibits ancient artifacts.
- **近义词**: display, show
- **派生词**: exhibition (n.)

## expand
- **音标**: /ɪkˈspænd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 扩大；扩展
- **例句**: The company plans to expand into new markets.
- **近义词**: grow, extend
- **派生词**: expansion (n.)

